<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław III the Generous</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1291">1291</a>–<a href="/years/1352">1352</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław III the Generous was a Silesian Piast duke, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-the-fat">Henry V of Legnica</a>. In 1311 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a> on the Oder as his share of the inheritance, creating the Duchy of Brzeg, and he also held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> for a time. In 1329 he did homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, bringing his duchy under the Bohemian crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-the-generous.jpg" alt="Bolesław III the Generous" width="320" height="732" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albrecht Bräuer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boleslaus_von_Liegnitz.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
